1. PVT CORNER SUMMARY TABLE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Corner | Condition          | Setup Slack | Setup Status | Hold Slack | Hold Status | Max Frequency (Fmax)
-------+--------------------+-------------+--------------+------------+-------------+---------------------
tt     | 1.80V, 25C (Typ)   |  +0.070 ns  | MET          | +0.300 ns  | MET         | 134.59 MHz (7.43 ns)
ss     | 1.60V, 100C (Slow) |  -2.820 ns  | VIOLATED*    | +0.450 ns  | MET         |  96.89 MHz (10.32 ns)
ff     | 1.95V, -40C (Fast) |  +2.550 ns  | MET          | +0.120 ns  | MET         | 202.02 MHz (4.95 ns)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

*Note on Slow Corner Signoff:
The 7.50 ns (133.33 MHz) timing constraint was closed specifically at the nominal
tt_025C_1v80 operating point. In silicon manufacturing, high junction temperature (100C)
and reduced core rail voltage (1.60V, -11% VDD) increase standard cell switching delays by
~38%. To guarantee timing closure across full industrial temperature and supply variations,
the operational clock should be derated to 95.0 MHz (Tclk = 10.5 ns), or synthesis resizer
effort must target 5.2 ns at tt.

2. HOLD TIMING VERIFICATION (FAST CORNER ff_n40C_1v95)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Hold verification checks race conditions between clock arrival and data arrival.
At fast-fast corner, combinational logic speeds up significantly.
- Minimum Path Hold Slack: +0.120 ns (MET)
- Hold WNS:               0.000 ns
- Hold TNS:               0.000 ns
Conclusion: Zero hold violations exist across the entire register file and pipeline
at extreme fast-process conditions.

